Subject: [PATCH 6/9] build(deploy): target a Node server (Vercel), drop GitHub
 Pages static export

The app has server-only features (contact API route, next-intl proxy, and
cookie-gated analytics) that a static export to GitHub Pages silently breaks.
Path A: deploy to a Node host instead, which makes all three work.

- next.config.ts: remove output:export, trailingSlash, basePath/assetPrefix
  and images.unoptimized (all GitHub-Pages-only). Keep safe SVG handling.
- Remove .github/workflows/deploy.yml and scripts/gh-pages-postbuild.mjs;
  drop the postbuild npm script. Vercel deploys via its Git integration.
- Add .github/workflows/ci.yml (lint + typecheck + build) as a quality gate.
- Add a typecheck script; document NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID in .env.example.
- Fix stale 'required for output: export' comments.

Verified with a full `next build`: /api/contact and Proxy (Middleware) are
now part of the build output.
